  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Mountain song of northern Shaanxi and the neighbouring Loess Plateau, sung by drovers, carters and farm workers out on the hills. Each song is built from rhyming couplets of an upper and a lower line, often opening with an image from nature, repeated with new words; it is the best-known genre of Shaanbei folk song, which is listed on China's national intangible-heritage register.",
